WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.062
Why a standard?

2
00:00:01.062 --> 00:00:05.157
Module 12 moved one account,
with Microsoft Learn's commands,

3
00:00:05.157 --> 00:00:07.450
and the kit planned the same moves.

4
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.672
The standard makes every managed service
account after that go the same way:

5
00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:15.158
asked for, approved, created, watched,

6
00:00:15.158 --> 00:00:18.888
attested and retired, with
the same evidence each time.

7
00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:20.937
It splits the work three ways.

8
00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:25.788
SailPoint approves, reached through the
agency's system access management tool.

9
00:00:25.788 --> 00:00:29.013
ServiceNow records the
change and the findings.

10
00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:31.846
And Microsoft's tools create and enforce:

11
00:00:31.846 --> 00:00:37.182
Active Directory PowerShell through
Chapter 6's approved plan, Group Policy,

12
00:00:37.182 --> 00:00:41.900
Defender for Identity and, when the
workload moves, Microsoft Entra.
